From 845228ac056222ee72b85b686157cf30658ebace Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:05:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plasma): Plasma Profile takes a start pick and an exit
 pick

The Plasma Profile now reads the operation-level picks (#3339). Its pick
capability is Ring.

- Start pick: the lead-in of the nearest closed contour lands on the
  projection of the pick on the profile. The pierce is at the start of
  that lead-in, in the scrap.
- Exit pick: the torch cuts the full contour, then cuts on to the
  projection of the exit pick. The lead-out and the torch off are there.
- The small-hole rule keeps its centre pierce, its overburn and its
  missing lead-out under a pick.
- A pick that a law cannot hold is refused by name, never moved: too far
  from each closed profile, open runs only, no lead room at the pick, a
  small-hole lead-in across the part, an exit inside the overburn, an
  exit pick with control compensation (G41/G42).
- A cut without a pick is the same path, move for move.

The waterjet kind keeps its "not taken" answer. Its slice is a follow-up.

Fixes #3334

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
